      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-04T23:33:11.327+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "but yeah, for improving PSRR, active filter in front to limit the input voltage to more limited range should help a lot.>\nif you make that one start up transparent/pass-active it should do great.\nConsider using the native NMOS for that actually, like, with a pull-up resistor from gate to drain, and once the vref is active, you can compare a resistor division of the LDO output against vref and pull the gate down if the resistor division is too high (relatively).",
